From 8e71a346d71c81ad9e3d26922dad656e14d15983 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:26:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: declare the hostapd HAL (Wi-Fi hotspot)

Android 10 starts hostapd only through its HIDL interface: the framework
calls IHostapd::getService() and hwservicemanager launches the daemon
from the interface lines in hostapd.android.rc. The manifest did not
declare android.hardware.wifi.hostapd, so the lookup failed ("Cannot find
entry ... in either framework or device manifest"), the framework gave
up after 5 s ("Failed to connect to hostapd") and the hotspot switch
turned itself off again. Declared at 1.1, the version our hostapd
registers. The Wi-Fi HAL already moves the built-in prima driver to AP
mode (it writes "ap" to the wlan fwpath parameter; con_mode becomes 1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 manifest.xml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/manifest.xml b/manifest.xml
index e559a34..a0ddfb0 100644
--- a/manifest.xml
+++ b/manifest.xml
@@ -261,6 +261,15 @@ included.
             <instance>default</instance>
         </interface>
     </hal>
+    <hal format="hidl">
+        <name>android.hardware.wifi.hostapd</name>
+        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
+        <version>1.1</version>
+        <interface>
+            <name>IHostapd</name>
+            <instance>default</instance>
+        </interface>
+    </hal>
     <hal format="hidl">
         <name>com.qualcomm.qti.imscmservice</name>
         <transport>hwbinder</transport>
